  "strategy": "Approach and Rationale:  \nMinimize \\(2n \\max(\\text{conv}(a, a)) / (\\sum a)^2\\) with \\(a \\geq 0\\) by:  \n1. Leveraging gradient descent in logarithmic space to handle arbitrary coefficient ranges efficiently.  \n2. Using importance sampling to transition between dimensions where the search space is restructured in hypergeometric progression.  \n3. Solving a linear program (LP) to directly control convolution extrema via coordinate transformation.  \nThe algorithm iteratively improves the sequence by alternating between gradient-based updates in log-space and dimension-adjusted insertions through tentative inflation schemes.  \n\nMathematical Specification:  \n- Input sequence from `height_sequence_1` (if available) or start from a uniform random.  \n- Dominate the sequence space using the normalized simplex representation via \\( \\log(a_i) \\).  \n- The objective is a scale-invariant ratio between \\( 2n \\max(\\text{conv}) \\) and \\( S^2 = (\\sum a_i)^2 \\).  \n- Constraints include: non-negativity maintained by \\( \\max(0, \\cdot) \\), sum normalization to \\([0.001, 1000]\\), and evolution pathways shaped by a multi-stage optimization.  \n- Hyperparameters include:  \n  - Peak thinning rate \\( \\beta \\in (0.001, 0.1) \\)  \n  - Target sum \\( S = 64.0 \\) (arbitrary scale enforcement)  \n  - Time budget allocation \\( T = 1800 \\) seconds  \n\nImplementation Procedure:  \n1. If `height_sequence_1` is provided, normalize and use its length \\( n = \\text{len}(\\text{height\\_sequence\\_1}) \\).  \n2. Otherwise, default to length \\( 512 \\).  \n3. Setup:  \n   - Initialize using a target sequence via `_make_flat_spectrum_init`,  \n   - Define optimization bounds in log-space for adaptive tuning.  \n4. Iterative Core:  \n   - Gradient descent (Adam) on log-space coordinates,  \n   - Evaluate \\( \\text{score} = 2.0 \\cdot n \\cdot \\max(\\text{conv}) / S^2 \\) periodically via exact validation,  \n   - Insert dimension-adjustments:  \n     * Expand as \\( n = 2n \\) if under-utilized,  \n     * Contract as \\( n = n/1.4 \\) if plateau found,  \n     through explicit simplex projections.  \n5. Phase Transitions:  \n   - After 30% time completion, switch to dimension variable,  \n   - At 50% time, switch from expansion to contraction logic.  \n\nSearch Choices and Useful Variations:  \n- Coordinate beta-adaptive system for peak avoidance.  \n- Expanded dimensions (768) if parent's length falls below density targets.  \n- Contraction to smaller dimensions (512) if overparameterized.  \n- Convergence metrics: decrease rate of scoring improvement \\( \\geq 1e-7 \\).  \n- Prevention of optimization stuck points via random restarts every 100 iterations.  \n\nCompute Budget and Robustness:  \n- Total time: 6 minutes per optimization suspect (3 if multiple lengths).  \n- Time per convolution: \\( O(n \\log n) \\) with bounds checking.  \n- Budget allocation:  \n  1. Run-time safety: 1 second buffer for initialization/normalization.  \n  2. Periodic validation: every 0.6 seconds to hit hard time bounds.  \n- Component-wise recomposition: separate peak adjustment and LP-based blends.  \n\nValidation and Return Contract:  \n- Maintain a running best sequence \\( best\\_a \\) with adaptive rescaling.  \n- Exact evaluation using `evaluate_sequence` before accepting a record.  \n- Integrated safety: clips negatives via \\( \\max(0, \\cdot) \\) and caps at 1000.  \n- Formatting: always return the best sequence as `[float(x) for x in sequence]`.  \n- Fallback: uniform random sequence if optimization stalls.",
